hi Matt Welch here with nick gillespie  we're here on ask a libertarian day in  honor of the paperback publication of  the Declaration of Independence how  libertarian politics can fix what's  wrong with America next question comes  from case on white via email do you  believe there's a growing income gap if  so do you believe its problem and what  is the libertarian approach to fixing it  Nick yeah there is a growing amount of  inequality when you look at the very  richest and the very poorest that gap  has been widening in the United States  as it has through all developed  countries is it a problem I don't think  so in and of itself the real question is  income mobility what are the odds of one  person particularly those towards the  bottom of the distribution can move up  the distribution all of the data that is  relevant show that income mobility has  not decreased over the past 40 or so  years that's the real issue income  mobility not income inequality and I  always get upset when people confuse or  conflate those two things they're very  different things if we want more income  mobility and I do because I still have a  long way to go up and I want my kids  both to be able to go up or go down  based on how they act and the choices  that they make in their life I'm because  that's a better system for more people  when you can actually get the rewards to  your benefits the way we do that is by  minimizing government by streamlining  the ways in which people can find their  way in the world and instead of trying  to rig the game so that certain types of  people get a leg up for doing certain  types of activities let's flatten it out  a bit more the most unequal societies  I've ever seen are those that are  currently or recently communist everyone  is supposed to be equal but the gnomon  clap Torah above it all has perks that  everybody else can't even dream of I  don't think equality ultimately is the  goal equality of opportunity is the best  that we can shoot towards that is Matt  Welch talking about ask a libertarian  day 2012 we will be here all day and  we'll be taking your questions thanks
 

